WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
Hey, welcome back.

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.580
Last time, a changing magnetic field created an induced emf.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.300
Today the field can stay constant while a conductor moves.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.660
Picture a vertical metal rod moving to the right through a uniform field into

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:15.140
the page.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.840
Charges inside the rod share its motion.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.740
The magnetic force on a positive charge is q times velocity cross B.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.020
Use your right hand: right crossed with into the page points upward.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.920
Positive charge accumulates near the upper end, and electrons shift toward the

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.360
lower end.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.560
The upper end becomes positive.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.600
This separation creates a downward electric field.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.460
In the ideal open circuit steady state, electric and magnetic forces balance

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.160
along the rod.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.640
The electric field magnitude is v B, so the voltage magnitude across a rod of

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.000
length l is B l v.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.980
This shortcut assumes the rod, velocity and field are mutually perpendicular

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.400
and the motion is uniform across the rod.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.960
More generally, the motional contribution is the line integral of velocity

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.140
cross B dotted with the length element.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.120
Do not multiply three magnitudes when the geometry does not support it.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.360
For B equal to zero point five tesla, length zero point four meter and speed

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.680
three meters per second, the voltage is zero point six volt.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.300
There is no complete external circuit, so no sustained circulating current.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.800
Voltage and current are different questions.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.780
Reverse the motion or the field, and the end polarity reverses.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.472
Now place the same moving rod across two horizontal conducting rails,

00:01:32.472 --> 00:01:33.060
connected

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.960
through a resistor on the left.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.800
The rod completes a circuit.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.380
As it moves right, the enclosed rectangle grows wider.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.360
Its area is rod length times position x, so the magnitude of flux is B times l

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.060
times x.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.300
Differentiate with respect to time.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:55.680
Since the rate of change of x is speed v, the induced emf magnitude is B l v.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.560
The charge force picture and the changing flux picture agree.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.440
Let's get direction without guessing.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.820
The field goes into the page, and the circuit area grows.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.560
Inward flux is increasing.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.660
Lenz's law requires an outward induced field, which corresponds to

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.680
counterclockwise conventional current when viewed facing the page.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.160
Along the right hand moving rod, that current goes upward.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.360
Along the top rail it goes left.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.140
Use our previous numbers: field zero point five tesla, rod length zero point

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.700
four meter and speed three meters per second.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.240
Emf is zero point six volt.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.180
If the total circuit resistance is two ohms, current is zero point three

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:33.700
ampere.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.400
We assume good sliding contacts, negligible lead resistance beyond the stated

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.880
total, and negligible self inductive effects.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:45.240
Immediately after a sudden change, appreciable inductance could alter the

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:45.840
current response.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.400
In this elementary resistive model, emf divided by resistance is appropriate.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.820
Opening the connection stops the sustained loop current even though the moving

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.900
rod can still develop an end to end voltage.

00:02:57.408 --> 00:03:01.348
Current is now flowing, so the rod experiences a magnetic force.

00:03:02.268 --> 00:03:04.468
Current points up and field points into the page.

00:03:05.148 --> 00:03:07.068
Up crossed with into the page points left.

00:03:07.728 --> 00:03:10.048
That force opposes the rod's rightward motion.

00:03:10.768 --> 00:03:14.728
To maintain constant speed, an external agent must pull right with equal

00:03:14.728 --> 00:03:17.588
magnitude, if friction and other forces are neglected.

00:03:18.548 --> 00:03:22.168
The magnetic force magnitude is current times rod length times field.

00:03:22.788 --> 00:03:28.088
Substitute current B l v over R and you obtain B squared times l squared times

00:03:28.088 --> 00:03:28.968
v over R.

00:03:29.948 --> 00:03:31.428
Let's calculate with the same circuit.

00:03:32.348 --> 00:03:36.484
Current is zero point three ampere, length zero point four meter and field

00:03:36.484 --> 00:03:36.708
zero

00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:37.688
point five tesla.

00:03:38.508 --> 00:03:40.448
The drag force is zero point zero six newton.

00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:44.728
At speed three meters per second, the pulling power is zero point one eight

00:03:44.728 --> 00:03:45.028
watt.

00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:49.248
Now calculate electrical heating: current squared times resistance.

00:03:50.048 --> 00:03:53.348
Zero point three squared times two is also zero point one eight watt.

00:03:53.348 --> 00:03:56.028
Lovely: the energy accounts match.

00:03:56.728 --> 00:04:00.188
The resistor's heating comes from mechanical work, not an inexhaustible

00:04:00.188 --> 00:04:01.248
magnetic energy gift.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.508
At constant speed, kinetic energy is unchanged.

00:04:05.128 --> 00:04:09.468
If you release the rod, this simple model predicts deceleration as mechanical

00:04:09.468 --> 00:04:10.928
energy is converted into heat.

00:04:11.208 --> 00:04:14.888
The drag decreases with speed; it is not a fixed friction force.

00:04:14.888 --> 00:04:19.628
Doubling speed with the other quantities fixed doubles current and force, but

00:04:19.628 --> 00:04:20.788
quadruples heating power.

00:04:21.468 --> 00:04:24.168
Those different scaling laws are useful JEE checks.

00:04:25.272 --> 00:04:27.292
Here is a trap worth slowing down for.

00:04:27.932 --> 00:04:31.472
A rectangular conducting loop moves right into a region with uniform magnetic

00:04:31.472 --> 00:04:32.612
field into the page.

00:04:33.452 --> 00:04:35.832
Does motion always mean a nonzero net emf?

00:04:36.392 --> 00:04:36.732
No.

00:04:37.472 --> 00:04:40.152
During entry, the area of the loop inside the field increases.

00:04:40.792 --> 00:04:45.313
If its vertical side length is w, the overlapping area grows at rate w times

00:04:45.313 --> 00:04:45.432
v.

00:04:46.072 --> 00:04:49.272
The emf magnitude is B w v.

00:04:49.992 --> 00:04:54.057
Inward flux increases, so current is counterclockwise as viewed facing the

00:04:54.057 --> 00:04:54.332
page.

00:04:54.792 --> 00:05:00.012
Once the entire rigid loop is inside the uniform, static field, its area and

00:05:00.012 --> 00:05:00.792
orientation remain fixed.

00:05:01.552 --> 00:05:04.412
Flux is constant, so net induced emf is zero.

00:05:05.292 --> 00:05:07.952
Opposite side motional contributions cancel around the loop.

00:05:08.812 --> 00:05:12.292
Charges may redistribute locally, but this does not create a sustained loop

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:14.252
current in our resistive steady state model.

00:05:14.892 --> 00:05:17.232
As the loop exits, inward flux decreases.

00:05:17.852 --> 00:05:19.052
The current becomes clockwise.

00:05:19.692 --> 00:05:24.192
Try field zero point four tesla, vertical width zero point three meter and

00:05:24.192 --> 00:05:25.372
speed two meters per second.

00:05:26.352 --> 00:05:29.512
Entry or exit emf magnitude is zero point two four volt.

00:05:30.532 --> 00:05:34.692
With total resistance one point two ohms and negligible inductance, current

00:05:34.692 --> 00:05:36.752
magnitude is zero point two ampere.

00:05:37.152 --> 00:05:38.552
Fully inside, current is zero.

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:43.032
The ideal abrupt boundaries separate three regimes; real field edges are

00:05:43.032 --> 00:05:43.292
smoother.

00:05:44.072 --> 00:05:47.741
Mechanical drag acts while flux is changing, not throughout every uniform

00:05:47.741 --> 00:05:47.992
field

00:05:47.992 --> 00:05:48.532
translation.

00:05:49.352 --> 00:05:52.812
Check overlap area before using B l v for the net circuit emf.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.660
A circuit does not always need visible wires.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.900
A solid metal plate contains many possible closed conducting paths.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:05.360
If linked magnetic flux changes through those paths, circulating currents can

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.580
form inside the plate.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.680
We call them eddy currents.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.940
Picture a conducting plate moving through a localized magnetic field.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.400
Different parts enter and leave the field region, so the linked flux changes.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.880
The induced currents interact with the field and can oppose the motion,

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.540
converting mechanical energy into heat.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.420
This gives magnetic damping without rubbing surfaces together.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.860
But do not claim that any metal moving anywhere in a uniform static field must

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.380
experience eddy current braking.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.500
Geometry and changing linked flux matter.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:44.240
A stationary ordinary conductor in a static field does not continuously

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.320
generate eddy currents.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:49.180
A changing applied field can induce them even without motion.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:54.480
For transformer cores, unwanted circulating currents waste energy as heat.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:59.880
Thin insulated laminations interrupt large conducting paths and reduce those

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:00.060
losses.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.950
Slots in a conducting plate can similarly weaken damping by obstructing

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:05.320
current

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:05.680
paths.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.200
These methods reduce currents; they do not abolish electromagnetic induction

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:10.780
itself.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.440
Induction heating deliberately uses changing fields to transfer energy into a

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:17.000
conducting workpiece.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.400
The power supply provides that energy.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.920
We will not assign one universal B l v circuit to an entire plate: its current

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:28.720
distribution depends on shape, conductivity and field variation.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:34.560
Your final checklist is motion geometry, flux change, closed paths, resistance

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.820
and the energy source.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:39.740
That is how the rod and the plate belong to the same physical story.
